      "motion": null,
      "microAnimations": [],
      "body": "A job search's page is its conversation with your AI coach: it has the job offers found and their Match Scores with the profile in view. Until you have written anything, suggestions wait above the message box: « Which offers to pick? », « Widen my criteria », « Search again ».\n\nOn the right, the search's fiche: its status, the day it started and the profile's search criteria, which « Change the criteria » opens, then « Search again », or « Stop the search » while it is searching. The panel's « Job offers found » view shows each job offer found with its Match Score; the « Job offers found » section, in the fiche, lists them all. A job offer you already saved carries the label « Saved »; a job offer you set aside in « Offers to handle » carries the label « Set aside »: it can still be read, and « Go back on this choice », in « Set aside », puts it back to handle.\n\nThe activity shows the search while it runs, then the page's history, in the order of time: the search, with the quota it used (« 1 search from your plan », with the week's use) and the offers it kept, the offers it read, each « ↳ follows » the search, and the coach's replies in this conversation. Each row opens on its detail and leads to its page or its message.\n\nA job offer opens beside the conversation, without hiding it, with its score, what explains it, and « Save as an application » to follow it in your applications. « Close » or the Escape key closes it.\n\nThe offers you receive by email for this profile are not among a search's results: they are in « Received by email », on the Job searches page.\n\nOn a phone, the conversation takes the whole screen. « Fiche » opens the panel over it, full screen, the other views are under « … », and a job offer opens full screen too: « Close » or « Close the panel » closes them and brings you back to the conversation.\n\nIn the Jobbbox app (iPhone, iPad, Android), a search's page shows its fiche above its conversation: its status, the day it started and the profile's search criteria, to read; « Change the criteria » opens the profile's page of jobbbox.ai in the app. Once the search has ended, « Search again » starts a new one for the same profile, within your plan's quota: when it is used, the app says so as jobbbox.ai does, with nothing to buy. Its job offers follow, closest to your master CV first, each marked « Followed » or « Set aside » when it is. Tap one to open it: its Match Score against the profile, a button explaining the score detailing each criterion, its summary and its text. « Follow » creates its application with this profile; once followed, « See the application » opens it. « Set aside » takes it out of your « Offers to handle », with a reason if you wish, and « Undo » goes back on it; a job offer set aside keeps « Go back on this choice »."
